Subject: dts: be7000: do not vote the MP5496 l2 regulator over RPM

The l2 node came from the IPQ9574 RDP boards, where l2 is the 1.8 V
supply of the USB PHY PLLs. With it the kernel sends an RPM request for
l2 at boot. The stock firmware never votes any RPM rail. On part of the
boards that request kills the receive side of the UNIPHY0 <-> QCA8084
10G-QXGMII lane: the SoC gets no block lock, PRBS31 from the chip is
all errors, while every UNIPHY, XPCS, SerDes and clock register reads
the same as on stock. Removing only the l2 node fixes the lane on such
a board (zerc00l, bisected: clk_ignore_unused alone and s1 >= 875 mV
alone do not help; iperf3 941 Mbit/s both ways, no lane errors). The
USB PHYs get a fixed 1.8 V regulator instead, l2 stays at the level
the bootloader set.

Qualcomm's own patch for the reference board says l2 is 850 mV, not
1800 mV, and that 1800 mV affected the stability of the networking
subsystem (patchwork 14128430, changes requested, never merged). Mainline
4f4c905e6a2a states that the USB PHYs use l5 and that l2 was specified for
them by mistake. The BE7000 RPM gave us no usable l5: pointing the USB PHYs
at it failed with -ENXIO, took the whole mp5496 regulator set down, s1 (CPU)
included, and USB never probed (tested on zerc00l). Stock describes neither
l2 nor l5 and gives the USB PHYs no supplies, so a fixed regulator it is.

--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9574-be7000.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9574-be7000.dts
@@ -38,6 +38,15 @@
 		bootargs-append = " ubi.block=0,ubi_rootfs root=/dev/ubiblock0_1 cpufreq.default_governor=powersave ubi.mtd=overlay mtdoops.mtddev=crash mtdoops.record_size=65536";
 	};
 
+	regulator_fixed_1p8: s1800 {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+		regulator-boot-on;
+		regulator-always-on;
+		regulator-name = "fixed_1p8";
+	};
+
 	regulator_fixed_3p3: s3300 {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
@@ -306,13 +315,6 @@
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <725000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1075000>;
 		};
-
-		mp5496_l2: l2 {
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
-			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
-			regulator-always-on;
-			regulator-boot-on;
-		};
 	};
 };
 
@@ -931,7 +933,7 @@
 };
 
 &usb_0_qmpphy {
-	vdda-pll-supply = <&mp5496_l2>;
+	vdda-pll-supply = <&regulator_fixed_1p8>;
 	vdda-phy-supply = <&regulator_fixed_0p925>;
 
 	status = "okay";
@@ -939,7 +941,7 @@
 
 &usb_0_qusbphy {
 	vdd-supply = <&regulator_fixed_0p925>;
-	vdda-pll-supply = <&mp5496_l2>;
+	vdda-pll-supply = <&regulator_fixed_1p8>;
 	vdda-phy-dpdm-supply = <&regulator_fixed_3p3>;
 
 	status = "okay";
